From: Nobara Project <nobara@protonmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] screencast: tell the chooser which session it is choosing for

The chooser runs synchronously for one ScreenCast session. Export that
session's handle as XDPW_CHOOSER_SESSION while it runs, so a chooser can
ask the requesting application's session for an explicit target instead
of relying on a global "next request" selection that a concurrent
request from another application could consume.
---
--- a/src/screencast/screencast.c
+++ b/src/screencast/screencast.c
@@ -163,7 +163,13 @@ bool setup_target(struct xdpw_screencast_context *ctx, struct xdpw_session *sess, st
 		target_initialized = xdpw_wlr_target_from_data(ctx, target, data);
 	}
 	if (!target_initialized) {
+		/* The chooser can ask this request's owner for an explicit target.
+		 * Never use a global "next request" selection: another application's
+		 * portal request may be queued concurrently. Selection is synchronous
+		 * here; the child inherits only this session's context. */
+		setenv("XDPW_CHOOSER_SESSION", sess->session_handle, 1);
 		target_initialized = xdpw_wlr_target_chooser(ctx, target, type_mask);
+		unsetenv("XDPW_CHOOSER_SESSION");
 		//TODO: Chooser option to confirm the persist mode
 		const char *env_persist_str = getenv("XDPW_PERSIST_MODE");
 		if (env_persist_str) {
